sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor S as Student
    actor R as Reviewer (instructor/admin)
    participant GW as Kong :8080
    participant ID as ms-identity :8081
    participant AZ as ms-authorization :8082
    participant CFG as ms-configuration :8087
    participant PG as PostgreSQL schema configuration
    participant BIO as ms-biometric :8086
    participant M as MongoDB biometric_update_cases

    Note over CFG,M: Verified 2026-10 against FULL — these are two fully independent implementations of the update-request feature, not a canonical store plus a mirror. Nothing in the code calls between ms-configuration and ms-biometric here — endpoint-matrix.md calling the biometric side a thin proxy of the canonical case is wrong

    rect rgb(238, 245, 238)
    Note over S,PG: 1. Path A — the documented "canonical" route
    S->>GW: POST /api/v1/biometric-update-cases {personId, biometricType, fingerNumber?, reason}
    GW->>ID: edge pre-function: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}
    ID-->>GW: 200 Active
    GW->>CFG: forward
    CFG->>ID: own guard: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}
    ID-->>CFG: Active, userId
    CFG->>AZ: GET /api/v1/auth/evaluate?permission=biometric.case:request
    AZ-->>CFG: allowed
    CFG->>CFG: resolveCaseScope — personId must be the caller's own unless they hold biometric.case:review
    alt biometricType = FINGERPRINT and fingerNumber missing
        CFG-->>S: 400 fingerNumber required for FINGERPRINT
    else valid
        CFG->>PG: INSERT biometric_update_case (updateStatus=Pending, requestedBy mandatory)
        CFG-->>S: 201 {caseId, updateStatus: Pending}
    end
    R->>GW: PATCH /api/v1/biometric-update-cases/{caseId}/review {updateStatus}
    GW->>CFG: forward (same guard chain, permission biometric.case:review)
    CFG->>PG: UPDATE (no ordering guard — see ST-03)
    CFG-->>R: 200 {updateStatus}
    end

    rect rgb(255, 246, 236)
    Note over S,M: 2. Path B — a second, independent implementation, same base path prefix
    S->>GW: POST /api/v1/biometric/update-request {person_id, biometric_type, reason}
    Note right of S: No fingerNumber field exists here at all — a FINGERPRINT case can be created with nothing to check it against
    GW->>ID: edge pre-function: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}
    ID-->>GW: 200 Active
    GW->>BIO: forward
    BIO->>ID: own guard: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}
    ID-->>BIO: Active
    BIO->>AZ: GET /api/v1/auth/evaluate?permission=biometric.case:request
    AZ-->>BIO: allowed
    Note right of BIO: No person-scope check like CFG's resolveCaseScope — any caller holding biometric.case:request may list or create for any person_id
    BIO->>M: insert document {request_id, person_id, status: Pending} — no requestedBy field anywhere in this entity
    BIO-->>S: 201 {request_id, status: Pending}
    R->>GW: PATCH /api/v1/biometric/update-request/{request_id}/review {status}
    GW->>BIO: forward (own guard, permission biometric.case:review)
    BIO->>M: update (no ordering guard either — same transitions as ST-03)
    BIO-->>R: 200 {status}
    end

    Note over CFG,M: The gap: a case filed through Path A is invisible to GET /api/v1/biometric/update-requests/{personId} (Path B), and a case filed through Path B is invisible to GET /api/v1/biometric-update-cases (Path A). A reviewer working from either endpoint sees only half of the real queue, and nothing detects or reconciles the split — see state-biometric-update.mmd for the per-store transition details
